# Data Access Architecture Standard

This project follows a Supabase + Direct PostgreSQL hybrid architecture.

## Core Principle

Supabase is a productivity layer.

PostgreSQL is the source of truth.

When business correctness matters, read from PostgreSQL.

## Use Supabase For

* Authentication
* Session Management
* User Accounts
* Realtime
* Presence
* Broadcast
* Realtime Subscriptions
* Storage
* Images
* Videos
* Documents
* User Uploads
* Non-critical reads
* Profiles
* Settings
* Static lists
* Catalog data

## Use Direct PostgreSQL For

* Wallet State
* Financial State
* Settlement Data
* Audit Data
* Room State
* Game State
* Tournament State
* Active Cards
* Active Players
* Room Population
* Winners
* Draw History
* Critical Counters
* Critical Snapshot APIs

## Snapshot APIs

Prefer PostgreSQL for:

* GET /gameroom
* GET /live-room
* GET /wallet
* GET /tournament

Do not use Supabase SDK as the sole source of truth for critical snapshots.

## Required Infrastructure

All projects must include:

* lib/db/postgres.ts
* lib/db/supabase.ts

and maintain two independent data-access paths.

## Debugging Rule

When investigating data inconsistencies:

1. Database
2. Direct PostgreSQL
3. Supabase SDK

Compare all three layers before drawing conclusions.

Never assume:

Supabase SDK == PostgreSQL

Treat Supabase as a convenience layer over PostgreSQL.

## Architecture Preference

When implementing new features:

* Use Supabase for productivity.
* Use PostgreSQL for certainty.
* Financial correctness always wins over convenience.

## Before Completing Any Data Task

Ask:

"Is this data business-critical or source-of-truth?"

If yes:
Prefer PostgreSQL.

If no:
Supabase is acceptable.
